1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Your spreadsheet. Your inventory. In sync.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Meet StockSheet.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Start with an Excel or CSV file.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Upload your sheet, then match its columns to your store.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Choose what to update, and select your inventory location.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Preview the changes before anything is applied.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Review unmatched rows and correct your sheet when needed.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
When everything looks right, confirm your changes.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Follow the progress as StockSheet updates your inventory.

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Open History to download your original spreadsheet or the results.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Undo can restore saved quantities,
while skipping stock that changed later.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
StockSheet. Less repetitive work.
More control over your stock.
